# A county's own ArcGIS FeatureServer. The county is the authoritative
# publisher of its own parcel geometry, so this is the trusted path.
#
# FRICTION (#13, zones): this topology exists ONLY to carry a `zone:` label,
# because `zone` is a topology-level key and there is no `zone` on a node. It
# wraps exactly one node and adds nothing else. That is ceremony -- three
# lines of wrapper per effect to say one word about the node inside.
#
# It also flattens a distinction I care about. "county-gis" is not one zone:
# it is five separate county governments' ArcGIS deployments, each with its
# own availability, its own field-name dialect, and in Roscommon's case its
# own known data bug. weir gives me one string per topology. To distinguish
# them I would need five single-node topologies, which is the (a) branch from
# routeCounty.node's comment showing up again by a different route.
#
# WHAT I WANT: `zone:` declarable on a `.node`, and a zone that can be a path
# ("county-gis/osceola") so queries can ask at either granularity.
zone: county-gis
input: DirectCountyQuery
output: RawParcelFeature
terminals:
  - fetchDirect
wiring:
  fetchDirect: {}
